      "summary": "parse_enabled is implemented as `return bool(value)` (src/parser.py). In Python, `bool(\"false\")` is True because any non-empty string is truthy, so the function returns True for the literal string \"false\". The test (checks/test_parser.py) asserts `parse_enabled(\"false\") is False`, which therefore fails. The repository contract (README.md) states the parser \"should recognize explicit true and false values,\" confirming the intended behavior is to map the string \"false\" to the boolean False, which the current `bool(value)` implementation does not provide."
